{%- comment -%}
  The talks posting switch: the ONE value that the composer, the reply box, Report, the pre-launch notice (TLK-153)
  and house rule 5 (TLK-075 live / TLK-154 pre-launch) all read, so they can never disagree. Outputs "on" or "off".
  Readers capture this snippet's output and compare it with "on" (see sections/st-talks-list.liquid), so its output must
  be exactly the value: a plain comment, no doc block. Turn it on only after the talks backend is set up and verified
  end to end (talks/OWNER-SETUP.md); talks/set_live.py flips it. The backend's own kill switch is talk_settings/main
  posting_open (TLK-130).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign st_talks_posting = 'on' -%}
